; A location carries rg's column, counted in characters from the line's
; start, and grep goes to it; a context line's column is 0.
> (system "mkdir -p ~/columns && printf 'h\\303\\251llo needle\\n  needle\\nafter\\n' > ~/columns/c.txt")
0
